ober 9 at 10:53AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"ESFGJT\n\nA strong low pressure system off the Pacific Coast will begin to draw\nin tropical moisture associated with Topical Storm Rachel this\nweekend. This strong southerly fetch will draw anomalously high\nmoisture content across the Desert Southwest and into eastern Utah\nand western Colorado. The chance for widespread precipitation\nincreases Saturday evening into Sunday. Total precipitation forecasts\nrange from 1 to 3 inches across high terrain, with highest amounts\nfavoring the Uintas, Tavaputs and the Southwest San Juan mountains.\n\nEmbedded thunderstorms are also possible Sunday afternoon, increasing\nthe threat for flash flooding across vulnerable terrain. While\nconfidence in location and rainfall rates remain low at this time,\nthe potential for rapidly rising rivers, streams, normally dry\narroyos and slot canyons are possible Sunday through Monday.\n\nPlease follow the evolving forecast, especially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-12T00:06:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 120006 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 606 PM MDT Sun Oct 11 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - An additional 1-2\" of rain is expected over the high terrain through Monday, with locally higher amounts likely over the Uintas. Flooding/flash flooding remains possible, but not probable. - A Wind Advisory is in effect through 6 AM Monday with valley wind","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-11T18:53:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Gusty winds up to 40-50 mph continue through the overnight hours, with showers and storms decreasing in intensity this evening. Wet weather remains in the forecast through at least mid week, with snow chances increasing over the higher terrain as the week progresses. Critical fire weather conditions are not anticipated, but watch out for windy conditions over the next handful of days","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":null,"airgradient":null,"airnow":null,"openmeteo_aq":{"pm25":0.6,"pm10":0.8,"co":108,"no2":0.5,"so2":0.1,"o3":68,"european_aqi":24,"us_aqi":34,"time":"2026-10-11T20:00"},"usgs":null,"snotel":null,"cdot_camera":{"id":"969","name":"US 40 MP 040.35 WB at Elk Spings Ranch","lat":40.37032,"lon":-108.389,"distance_km":50.1,"imageUrl":null,"pageUrl":"https://maps.cotrip.org/?lat=40.37032&lon=-108.389&zoom=12"},"cdot_rwis":null,"cdot_roads":{"updatedAt":"2026-10-12T03:36:39.383Z","alerts":[],"cameras":[{"id":"969","name":"US 40 MP 040.35 WB at Elk Spings Ranch","lat":40.37032,"lon":-108.389,"distance_km":50.1,"imageUrl":null,"pageUrl":"https://maps.cotrip.org/?lat=40.37032&lon=-108.389&zoom=12"}],"links":{"cotrip":"https://maps.cotrip.org"},"rwis":null,"road_condition":{"id":"198","name":"US 40, between the Utah Border (near Dinosaur) and Barclay Street (Craig)","routeName":"US 40","lat":40.273339381422375,"lon":-109.05101711367836,"condition":"dry","forecast_text":"Numerous Light Rain Showers. Isolated Thunderstorms. Wind gusts of up to 48 mph are expected.","observed":"